    <h1><a name="Computer Introduction">Computer Introduction</a></h1>
    <p>Computer ek electronic device hai jo user ke dwara diye gaye instructions ko follow karke data ko process karta hai, aur hume useful output deta hai. Ye machine binary language (0 aur 1) mein kaam karti hai, jise sirf electronic devices samajh sakti hain. Computer ka full form hota hai: Common Operating Machine Particularly Used for Technological and Educational Research, halanki ye ek acronymous definition hai, jo asal mein use nahi hoti. Computer ka use duniya ke har field mein ho raha hai jaise ki education, business, science, engineering, medicine, banking, aur even ghar ke kaamon mein bhi. Iske zariye hum documents bana sakte hain, internet chala sakte hain, games khel sakte hain, movies dekh sakte hain, aur data store karke rakha ja sakta hai. Aaj ke digital yug mein computer insaan ki life ka ek important part ban chuka hai. Har organization mein computer ki madad se kaam fast, accurate aur efficient ban gaya hai. Ye machine multitasking mein bhi expert hoti hai — ek samay par kai kaam kar sakti hai bina thake.

Computer ka development kai stages mein hua hai. Sabse pehle generation ke computers vacuum tubes par based the, jo bahut bade aur slow the. Aaj ke modern computers microprocessors par kaam karte hain jo chhote, fast aur powerful hote hain. Computer mainly do cheezon se milkar bana hota hai — Hardware (jo hum dekh sakte hain jaise monitor, keyboard, mouse, CPU) aur Software (jo hum dekh nahi sakte lekin kaam karne ke liye zaroori hota hai jaise Windows, MS Word, Chrome). Input devices se data liya jata hai, processing CPU mein hoti hai, aur output hume screen ya printer ke through milta hai. Aaj kal ke computers smart aur AI-enabled ho gaye hain jise hum voice, touch aur gestures se bhi control kar sakte hain. Aage chal kar Artificial Intelligence aur Quantum Computing jaise advanced techniques ke saath computers aur bhi powerful ban jaayenge. Computer ki knowledge aaj ke samay mein har kisi ke liye zaroori ho gayi hai — chaahe woh student ho, job seeker, ya businessman. Har field mein computer skills ek basic requirement ban chuki hai.</p>

<h3><a name="1. Central Processing Unit (CPU)">1. Central Processing Unit (CPU)</a></h3>
<p>CPU, yaani Central Processing Unit, ko computer ka “brain” kaha jaata hai. Ye ek aisi chip hoti hai jo har tarah ke instructions ko process karti hai. Jab bhi hum computer mein koi kaam karte hain — jaise typing, file open karna, ya game khelna — toh un sabhi tasks ko process karne ka kaam CPU karta hai. Ismein teen main parts hote hain: ALU (Arithmetic Logic Unit), CU (Control Unit) aur Registers. ALU basic calculations aur logical operations karta hai, CU instructions ko control karta hai aur Registers temporary data store karte hain. CPU ka speed "GHz (Gigahertz)" mein measure kiya jaata hai. Jitni zyada frequency, utna hi fast processor. Aaj kal Intel aur AMD jaise companies ke multi-core CPUs popular hain, jisme ek chip mein 2 se 16 tak cores hote hain jo ek saath multiple tasks ko process kar sakte hain. CPU bina kisi break ke lagataar kaam karta hai, lekin ye bahut heat bhi produce karta hai, isliye iske saath heat sink ya fan lagaya jaata hai. Ek powerful CPU poore system ke performance ko boost karta hai, isliye ye ek important aur essential part hai har computer ka.</p>
<h3><a name="2. Monitor (Display Screen)">2. Monitor (Display Screen)</a></h3>
<p>Monitor ek output device hai jo computer ke andar hone wale kaam ko visual form mein dikhata hai. Jab bhi hum computer pe koi kaam karte hain — jaise file open karna, video dekhna, ya game khelna — toh uska result hume monitor ke screen par hi dikhta hai. Pehle CRT (Cathode Ray Tube) monitors aate the jo bulky aur heavy hote the, lekin aaj kal ke monitors slim, light aur high-resolution wale LED aur LCD monitors hote hain. Monitor ka size inch mein measure kiya jata hai, jaise 15”, 21”, 27” etc. Resolution bhi important hota hai, jaise 1920x1080 (Full HD), 4K, ya 8K monitors. Monitors alag-alag purposes ke liye banaye jaate hain — basic kaam ke liye normal monitors, aur graphics designing ya gaming ke liye high refresh rate aur color-accurate monitors. Monitor ka interface VGA, HDMI, DisplayPort ya USB-C ke through CPU se connect hota hai. Touchscreen monitors bhi aate hain jisme mouse ya keyboard ki jagah finger ya stylus se input diya ja sakta hai. Monitor ek essential part hai bina jiske user computer ke output ko dekh hi nahi sakta.</p>
<h3>3. Keyboard</h3>
<p>Keyboard ek input device hai jiske through hum computer ko text, commands aur shortcuts provide karte hain. Isme kai keys hoti hain jo letters (A-Z), numbers (0-9), symbols (@, #, $, %, etc.), function keys (F1-F12), aur control keys (Ctrl, Alt, Shift) ka combination hota hai. Jab hum kisi key ko press karte hain, toh computer us signal ko read karke uske according output deta hai. Aaj kal keyboards wired aur wireless dono types ke available hain. Wireless keyboards Bluetooth ya USB receiver ke zariye connect hote hain. Mechanical keyboards zyada responsive hote hain aur gaming mein prefer kiye jaate hain, jabki membrane keyboards quiet aur soft typing ke liye hote hain. Ergonomic keyboards specially design kiye jaate hain jisse typing mein comfort mile aur hand strain na ho. Hindi typing ke liye Inscript ya Remington layout use hota hai. Shortcuts jaise Ctrl+C (copy), Ctrl+V (paste), aur Ctrl+Z (undo) ka use productivity badhane ke liye hota hai. Keyboard ke bina computer pe efficiently kaam karna mushkil hota hai, isliye ye ek core input device hai.

</p>
<h3>4. Mouse</h3>
<p>Mouse bhi ek input device hai jo mainly graphical user interface (GUI) mein navigation ke liye use hota hai. Jab hum mouse ko move karte hain, toh screen pe ek pointer ya cursor bhi move karta hai jise hum icons, files ya folders select karne ke liye use karte hain. Mouse mein usually 2 buttons (left & right) aur ek scroll wheel hota hai. Left click se selection ya commands execute ki jaati hain, right click se options open hote hain, aur scroll wheel se page up-down kiya jata hai. Aaj ke time mein optical mouse common hai jisme light sensor hota hai, jabki purane time ke ball mouse mechanical hote the. Wireless mouse Bluetooth ya USB dongle ke zariye connect hota hai. Gaming ke liye specially designed high DPI (dots per inch) mouse bhi milte hain jo zyada accurate aur fast response dete hain. Kuch mouse programmable hote hain jisme alag buttons ko alag functions assign kiya ja sakta hai. Touchpad bhi ek tarah ka mouse hi hota hai jo laptops mein hota hai. Mouse ke bina GUI-based system chalana mushkil hota hai, isliye ye ek zaroori input device hai.</p>
<h3>5. Motherboard</h3>
<p>Motherboard computer ka main circuit board hota ha i jisme sabhi hardware components directly ya indirectly connect hote hain. Ye ek platform provide karta hai jahan CPU, RAM, storage devices, GPU, aur aur bhi devices connect hote hain. Motherboard ka design aisa hota hai jisme alag-alag slots, ports aur sockets diye jaate hain — jaise CPU socket, RAM slots, PCIe slots (GPU ke liye), SATA ports (HDD/SSD ke liye), aur power connectors. Isme BIOS (Basic Input Output System) ya UEFI firmware hota hai jo system boot hone par basic functions control karta hai. Har motherboard ka chipset uski capability decide karta hai — jaise overclocking, RAM speed, USB support, aur storage options. Motherboard ke size ke mutabiq uska form factor hota hai: jaise ATX, Micro-ATX, Mini-ITX. Har computer ka performance motherboard ke quality aur compatibility par depend karta hai. Agar motherboard weak hai toh high-performance components bhi sahi se kaam nahi karenge. Isliye ye system ka backbone mana jaata hai.</p>
